From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael J. Ruhl" <michael.j.ruhl@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:17:58 -0700
Subject: [Temp] drm/xe/vsec: Correct locking order

Xe locking order is power state first, and then local locks.

Reorder locking for correct usage.

Signed-off-by: Michael J. Ruhl <michael.j.ruhl@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Rodrigo Vivi <rodrigo.vivi@intel.com>
(backported from https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/series/160717/#rev12)
Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vsec.c | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vsec.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vsec.c
index 481bcbcc6..1b88ac1d2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vsec.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vsec.c
@@ -157,16 +157,17 @@ int xe_pmt_telem_read(struct device *dev, u32 guid, u64 *data, loff_t user_offse
 
 	telem_addr += offset + user_offset;
 
-	guard(mutex)(&xe->pmt.lock);
-
 	/* indicate that we are not at an appropriate power level */
 	if (!xe_pm_runtime_get_if_active(xe))
 		return -ENODATA;
 
-	/* set SoC re-mapper index register based on GUID memory region */
-	xe->soc_remapper.set_telem_region(xe, mem_region);
+	scoped_guard(mutex, &xe->pmt.lock) {
+		/* set SoC re-mapper index register based on GUID memory region */
+		xe->soc_remapper.set_telem_region(xe, mem_region);
+
+		memcpy_fromio(data, telem_addr, count);
+	}
 
-	memcpy_fromio(data, telem_addr, count);
 	xe_pm_runtime_put(xe);
 
 	return count;
-- 
